\textbf{Solution}: From the given information, substituting point A$(2,2)$ into the inverse proportion function $y=\frac{m}{x}$, we get: $m=2\times 2=4$,\\
$\therefore y=\frac{4}{x}$. Then, substituting B$(3,n)$ into $y=\frac{4}{x}$, we find: $n=\frac{4}{3}$;\\
Hence, $m=\boxed{4}$, $n=\boxed{\frac{4}{3}}$;
